.idea/
.claude/
.superpowers/

node_modules/
out/
dist-installer/

# Build inputs that are fetched, not authored: the Host's runtime payload (a pinned node.exe and the
# files copied around it — scripts/host-runtime.mjs) and the download cache behind it. Pinned by
# version and SHA-256 in that script, so the bytes are reproducible without committing 90 MB.
resources/host-runtime/
build/.cache/

# docs/ is handled as a whitelist. Everything else there is design and planning notes that stay
# local — written this way round so a new note defaults to "not published".
docs/*
!docs/releasing.md
!docs/slack-bot-setup.md
!docs/jobs.md
!docs/how-it-works.md
!docs/usage-guide.md
# Published deliberately: a design brief that outlives the branch it was written on, because the work
# it describes is picked up in another session and often another worktree, where an ignored file does
# not exist. It says on its face that nothing in it is decided yet.
!docs/agent-workspace-isolation.md
# Published deliberately, for the same reason as the file above: the completion convergence loop is
# built from this design in another worktree, where an ignored file does not exist.
!docs/2026-09-19-completion-convergence-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the convergence UI is built from this design in another worktree.
!docs/2026-09-20-convergence-ui-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the session-failure visibility fix is built from this design.
!docs/2026-09-20-session-failure-visibility-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the convergence UI's second slice is built from this design.
!docs/2026-09-21-convergence-ui-slice2-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the convergence backend gaps are built from this design.
!docs/2026-09-21-convergence-backend-gaps-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the Job/Run split and the projects registry are built from this
# design over several sessions, and the public CLI is designed on top of the model it settles.
!docs/2026-09-21-job-run-split-and-projects-design.md
# Published deliberately, same reason: the public CLI is built from this design over several sessions.
!docs/2026-09-22-public-cli-design.md
# Published deliberately: the SignPath Foundation requires the code signing policy to be reachable at
# a public URL, and the README links to it.
!docs/code-signing.md
# Not a note but an input: scripts/build-release-notes.cjs reads docs/release-notes/<tag>.md out of
# the checkout the publish job makes at the tag, so a write-up that is not committed does not exist.
!docs/release-notes/

# The source brand sheet (a 1254x1254 mockup). Icons are cropped from it and only the outputs are
# committed — see scripts/gen-icon.ps1.
astera.png
